WEBVTT

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.064
This is Captain Kathryn Janeway

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.536
of the Starship Voyager.

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.300
We're responding
to your distress call.

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:09.569
A ruptured conduit
is flooding my ship

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:10.939
with plasma radiation.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.603
We request immediate transport.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:15.512
I'm detecting 11 life-signs;
two are weak.

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:17.550
Transport the injured
to Sick Bay

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:19.744
and the rest to Cargo Bay 1.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:22.083
I want security teams
at both locations.

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:30.318
Our weapons!

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:32.262
They'll be returned
to you when you leave.

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:34.527
These are dangerous criminals.
They have to be secured.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.967
We'll do our best
to accommodate you.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:38.766
I had eight men in custody.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.396
Where are the other two?

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:41.963
We're not going to hurt you.

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:43.700
Stay away, or I'll kill her!

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:38.950
I'm sure we can resolve this

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:40.855
without resorting
to violence.

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:42.758
What is it you want?

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:45.491
A ship, some food.

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:46.930
I might be able
to arrange that,

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.661
but you'll have
to release her first.

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:50.259
I'm not a fool.

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:55.736
You know I'll do it! Tell them.

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:57.503
You're not getting
off this ship.

00:02:57.577 --> 00:02:58.544
If you release her,

00:02:58.611 --> 00:03:00.203
I promise you
won't be harmed.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.874
Not until I get a ship.

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:04.348
We don't negotiate
with criminals.

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:05.475
Who are you?

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:08.316
Warden Yediq of the
Nygean Detention Force.

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:09.912
This man is my prisoner.

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:12.718
If that were true, he wouldn't
be holding my friend hostage.

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:17.760
Get back!

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:20.060
I'm a hologram.
I can't be harmed.

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:25.928
I think you proved my point.

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.835
We're lucky you came
along, Captain.

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:29.135
Ten more minutes

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:31.370
and none of us would have
survived the plasma leak.

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:33.173
Your vessel was equipped
with escape pods.

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:34.679
Why didn't you use them?

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:37.545
I couldn't risk letting
any of the prisoners get away.

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:39.915
As you've seen,
they're extremely dangerous.

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:41.112
Where are you taking them?

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:42.620
Back to our homeworld.

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:44.384
They're due to be executed.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:50.061
What were their crimes?

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:51.858
All eight are murderers.

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:54.058
Three are
multiple offenders.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.966
We're just 13 light-years
from our system.

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:59.402
I'd appreciate it
if you'd take us back there.

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:01.565
Actually, we were headed
in the opposite direction.

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:02.903
I could arrange

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:05.137
for one of our ships
to rendezvous with Voyager.

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:07.372
It'll take several days.

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:09.745
My prisoners will have
to be strictly monitored.

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:13.047
Commander Tuvok will help you
make arrangements.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.757
Some of the crew
may not be comfortable

00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:24.922
helping to deliver
eight men to their deaths.

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:27.262
I can't say I
like it, either...

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:30.302
but we have a Prime
Directive to follow.

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.633
30 more seconds,

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:36.470
and I could have resolved
the situation peacefully.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.669
Instead, you and "Tuvok the Kid"

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:40.872
had to take matters
into your own hands.

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:42.244
You're damaged.

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:44.878
Commander Tuvok's
friendly fire

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:46.043
must have caused

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:47.518
a feedback surge in my emitters.

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:48.679
I'll help you repair it.

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:52.190
How are you?

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:53.657
Fine, Captain.

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:55.523
You!

00:04:55.595 --> 00:04:57.187
This your ship?

00:04:57.263 --> 00:04:59.959
Yes.

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:02.591
Then let me out.

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:04.967
I'm afraid I can't do that.

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:19.049
If you don't, I'll kill you all.

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:21.920
Janeway to Tuvok.

00:05:22.055 --> 00:05:24.580
Are the prisoners'
accommodations ready?

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:26.386
Affirmative, Captain.

00:05:26.459 --> 00:05:29.656
Then by all means,
initiate transport.

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:38.060
You're sure
these will hold them?

00:05:38.137 --> 00:05:40.503
The force fields
are impenetrable,

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:42.438
as are the tritanium bulkheads.

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:43.941
In addition to your staff,

00:05:44.077 --> 00:05:45.840
two Voyager
security officers

00:05:45.912 --> 00:05:47.675
will remain here
at all times.

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:49.408
Two more will be posted

00:05:49.482 --> 00:05:51.882
at the entrance
to the cargo bay.

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:52.918
What about our weapons?

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:54.850
You'll be allowed
to carry them

00:05:54.921 --> 00:05:55.945
in this area only.

00:05:56.089 --> 00:05:57.716
If you leave the cargo bay,

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.758
you'll be asked
to surrender them.

00:05:59.826 --> 00:06:00.952
What's this?

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:02.153
Dinner.

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:04.753
Since you can't bring
the prisoners to the Mess Hall,

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:06.389
I brought the Mess Hall
to them.

00:06:06.466 --> 00:06:08.559
What is it?

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:11.899
Talaxian Spice Stew
served over leola rice pilaf.

00:06:12.038 --> 00:06:13.835
It's an old family recipe.

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:15.567
Take it back.

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:18.310
Too spicy?

00:06:18.378 --> 00:06:19.845
These men don't deserve

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:22.278
such an elaborate meal.

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:23.542
Take it back.

00:06:23.616 --> 00:06:25.550
Federation guidelines
are quite clear

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:27.381
about the treatment
of prisoners.

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:28.420
He is correct.

00:06:28.488 --> 00:06:29.750
I can quote the protocols,

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:31.346
if you like.

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:37.791
My men will assist you.

00:07:00.787 --> 00:07:02.584
Thanks for standing
up to Yediq.

00:07:02.655 --> 00:07:04.816
Just doing my job.

00:07:04.891 --> 00:07:06.119
Still,

00:07:06.192 --> 00:07:07.921
it was kind.

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:19.797
This would be easier
if you would remain stationary.

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:21.499
It doesn't feel right.

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:23.565
You may experience
unusual sensations

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:25.167
while your matrix realigns.

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:27.474
I was referring
to the "arrangement"

00:07:27.547 --> 00:07:29.811
the Captain's made
with the Nygeans.

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:32.510
No matter how terrible
the crimes these men committed,

00:07:32.585 --> 00:07:34.917
it seems wrong to hand them over
to be executed.

00:07:35.054 --> 00:07:37.921
This is a Federation starship,
not the Barge of the Dead.

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:40.015
Would you have preferred
the Captain release them?

00:07:40.092 --> 00:07:41.684
Of course not.
They're dangerous men.

00:07:41.761 --> 00:07:42.853
Executing them ensures

00:07:42.929 --> 00:07:44.658
they'll never pose a
threat to anyone again.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:48.029
So would life sentences...
the operative word being "life."

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:51.194
Confining them for life
requires significant resources.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.534
The Nygeans may not
think it worthwhile.

00:07:53.606 --> 00:07:54.800
What about rehabilitation?

00:07:54.874 --> 00:07:57.138
Given the chance,
some of these men might become

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:58.939
productive members
of society one day.

00:07:59.011 --> 00:08:01.980
Their victims won't have
the same opportunity.

00:08:02.048 --> 00:08:04.482
And that justifies
taking their lives?

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:07.018
An eye for an eye?

00:08:07.086 --> 00:08:09.213
It's not justice, it's revenge.

00:08:09.288 --> 00:08:11.051
Quite frankly, I'm surprised

00:08:11.123 --> 00:08:14.149
you're not troubled
by such a barbaric system.

00:08:14.227 --> 00:08:15.990
I'm simply being objective.

00:08:16.062 --> 00:08:17.461
You often encourage me

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:19.657
to see both sides
of an argument.

00:08:19.732 --> 00:08:21.700
Well...

00:08:21.767 --> 00:08:26.204
this is one occasion when
my programming won't allow me

00:08:26.272 --> 00:08:27.534
to be objective.

00:08:27.607 --> 00:08:31.065
Killing is wrong,
no matter who's doing it.

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:42.551
Still hungry?

00:08:42.622 --> 00:08:45.318
I can hear your
stomach from here.

00:08:45.391 --> 00:08:47.621
This must be
the first time in a month

00:08:47.693 --> 00:08:49.923
you couldn't steal
poor Egrid's meal.

00:08:52.732 --> 00:08:53.664
Good, isn't it?

00:08:53.733 --> 00:08:55.030
Mm-hmm.

00:09:06.145 --> 00:09:07.772
Is there a problem?

00:09:11.651 --> 00:09:14.620
Lko was just telling
me, he didn't get

00:09:14.687 --> 00:09:15.949
enough to eat.

00:09:17.757 --> 00:09:19.122
I see.

00:09:22.762 --> 00:09:24.787
Cause another disturbance

00:09:24.864 --> 00:09:26.195
and I'll see to it

00:09:26.265 --> 00:09:28.733
you're not fed
the rest of this journey.

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:29.768
Do you understand?

00:09:32.305 --> 00:09:35.069
Boche and Ledara...

00:09:35.141 --> 00:09:37.132
What did you say?

00:09:44.116 --> 00:09:46.107
Your children.

00:09:46.185 --> 00:09:47.743
How did you know that?

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:51.483
Are you sure they're safe?

00:09:51.557 --> 00:09:53.582
Some people don't understand

00:09:53.659 --> 00:09:56.492
why we deal so harshly
with men like you.

00:09:58.164 --> 00:10:00.894
It's because you never learn.

00:10:16.048 --> 00:10:17.276
Stand down!

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:20.410
Stand down!

00:10:20.486 --> 00:10:22.647
He needs to be disciplined.

00:10:22.722 --> 00:10:25.418
Lower your weapons
and step away.

00:10:42.975 --> 00:10:45.671
Our response was justified.

00:10:45.745 --> 00:10:48.373
How do you justify
beating a defenseless man?

00:10:48.447 --> 00:10:50.677
Violence is the only
thing he understands.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:54.345
You seem to have a pretty good
grasp of it yourself.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:56.820
Do not presume to tell me how
to handle my prisoners, Captain.

00:10:56.889 --> 00:10:59.824
You don't know lko like I do.

00:10:59.892 --> 00:11:02.224
He killed a young
father for no reason.

00:11:02.294 --> 00:11:05.388
Before that, he committed
dozens of violent crimes.

00:11:05.464 --> 00:11:07.932
He's spent his entire
life hurting people.

00:11:08.067 --> 00:11:10.797
That doesn't excuse
what you did to him.

00:11:12.438 --> 00:11:14.235
Until your transport vessel
gets here,

00:11:14.306 --> 00:11:16.934
you and your men won't be
allowed in the cargo bay.

00:11:17.043 --> 00:11:18.943
You're in charge
of the prisoners.

00:11:19.045 --> 00:11:20.569
Aye, Captain.

00:11:20.646 --> 00:11:22.204
They're my responsibility.

00:11:22.281 --> 00:11:23.908
Not as long
as you're aboard my ship.

00:11:23.983 --> 00:11:25.416
I won't risk any more violence.

00:11:25.484 --> 00:11:27.452
The only risk will
be to your crew.

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:29.283
Commander Tuvok
isn't qualified

00:11:29.355 --> 00:11:31.289
to guard prisoners
this dangerous.

00:11:31.357 --> 00:11:33.848
Tuvok has been
a Starfleet Security Officer

00:11:33.926 --> 00:11:35.154
for a very long time.

00:11:35.227 --> 00:11:37.718
Believe me, he's qualified.

00:11:37.797 --> 00:11:40.231
I hope you're right.

00:11:55.915 --> 00:11:57.906
You remember Mr. Iko.

00:11:57.983 --> 00:11:59.644
Vividly.

00:11:59.719 --> 00:12:02.882
The Nygeans decided to
make an example of him.

00:12:02.955 --> 00:12:04.354
Did you call me here

00:12:04.423 --> 00:12:07.153
to make a point
about Nygean barbarity?

00:12:07.226 --> 00:12:08.158
I called you here

00:12:08.227 --> 00:12:10.491
because I need your
help to save his life.

00:12:15.534 --> 00:12:17.866
He sustained a severe
blow to the head,

00:12:17.937 --> 00:12:19.404
which has caused severe edema

00:12:19.472 --> 00:12:20.530
in his parietal lobe.

00:12:20.606 --> 00:12:22.597
It's blocking vital
neurotransmitters.

00:12:22.675 --> 00:12:25.075
I'd like to program
some of your nanoprobes

00:12:25.144 --> 00:12:26.270
to bypass the edema.

00:12:29.281 --> 00:12:31.215
I'll comply.

00:12:31.283 --> 00:12:34.218
I sense a "but" coming.

00:12:34.286 --> 00:12:36.117
It seems inefficient
to save the life

00:12:36.188 --> 00:12:38.122
of someone
who's about to be executed.

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:40.124
If the Nygeans insist
on killing him,

00:12:40.192 --> 00:12:41.955
there isn't much
I can do about it,

00:12:42.061 --> 00:12:44.154
but I won't let them
do it on Voyager.

00:12:48.467 --> 00:12:51.698
I didn't expect to
see you back so soon.

00:12:53.472 --> 00:12:57.101
Ordinarily, we're lucky
to get one meal a day.

00:12:57.176 --> 00:12:59.508
That's terrible.

00:12:59.578 --> 00:13:02.513
Yediq likes to keep us hungry.

00:13:04.183 --> 00:13:07.414
Less talk. We're hungry!

00:13:07.486 --> 00:13:09.420
You're wondering why I'm here.

00:13:09.488 --> 00:13:11.649
Excuse me?

00:13:11.724 --> 00:13:15.490
You're wondering what I did
to end up with men like them.

00:13:17.496 --> 00:13:19.123
You killed someone?

00:13:21.634 --> 00:13:23.761
That's right.

00:13:28.474 --> 00:13:30.669
Why?

00:13:30.743 --> 00:13:32.506
Because I'm Benkaran.

00:13:32.578 --> 00:13:35.342
What does that have
to do with it?

00:13:39.585 --> 00:13:41.610
It's common knowledge

00:13:41.687 --> 00:13:43.951
that all Benkarans
are criminals,

00:13:44.023 --> 00:13:47.356
so when I was found
in the vicinity of a murder,

00:13:47.426 --> 00:13:49.360
I was immediately arrested.

00:13:49.428 --> 00:13:53.057
Are you saying you didn't do it?

00:13:53.132 --> 00:13:57.432
I told you, I'm Benkaran.

00:13:57.503 --> 00:14:01.303
What I say doesn't matter.

00:14:15.588 --> 00:14:18.022
You suffered
severe neurological trauma,

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:20.650
but I believe
we've repaired the damage.

00:14:23.295 --> 00:14:25.422
Thank you.

00:14:25.497 --> 00:14:28.330
Don't thank me.
Thank Seven of Nine.

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:32.234
She donated the nanoprobes
that saved your life.

00:14:32.304 --> 00:14:35.239
Oh, my head.

00:14:35.307 --> 00:14:36.274
The pain is normal.

00:14:36.342 --> 00:14:37.900
I'll prepare an analgesic.

00:14:43.449 --> 00:14:45.713
You're not afraid of me.

00:14:45.784 --> 00:14:49.550
There's no reason to fear
someone in your condition.

00:14:49.622 --> 00:14:51.783
You were never afraid of me,

00:14:51.857 --> 00:14:55.520
not even when I
tried to kill you.

00:14:55.594 --> 00:14:58.427
It's nice to look
into someone's eyes

00:14:58.497 --> 00:15:01.625
and not see fear.

00:15:09.508 --> 00:15:11.203
Do you have to be
a criminal to get

00:15:11.277 --> 00:15:12.801
something to eat
around here?

00:15:12.878 --> 00:15:16.041
Sorry. Dinner will be
ready in 15 minutes.

00:15:16.115 --> 00:15:18.640
You said that
15 minutes ago.

00:15:18.717 --> 00:15:21.811
Did you know the Nygeans
govern a sector of space

00:15:21.887 --> 00:15:24.879
occupied by several
different humanoid species?

00:15:24.957 --> 00:15:26.925
If we say yes,
will you feed us?

00:15:27.026 --> 00:15:30.052
One of those species
is the Benkarans.

00:15:30.129 --> 00:15:35.294
They occupy just ten
percent of Nygean space,

00:15:35.367 --> 00:15:39.701
but take up nearly 80 percent
of the space in Nygean prisons.

00:15:39.772 --> 00:15:43.230
Maybe they commit
more crimes.

00:15:43.309 --> 00:15:45.834
Not according to Joleg,
one of the prisoners.

00:15:45.911 --> 00:15:47.674
You think he was given
a harsher sentence

00:15:47.746 --> 00:15:49.270
because of his species?

00:15:49.348 --> 00:15:50.542
According to this,

00:15:50.616 --> 00:15:52.584
Benkarans are ten times
more likely

00:15:52.651 --> 00:15:55.279
to be executed for their crimes
than Nygeans.

00:15:55.354 --> 00:15:56.378
Where'd you get that?

00:15:56.455 --> 00:15:58.082
I contacted the
Nygean government.

00:15:58.157 --> 00:15:59.419
Told them I was interested

00:15:59.491 --> 00:16:00.617
in a cultural exchange.

00:16:00.693 --> 00:16:02.888
Among other things,
they let me access data

00:16:03.028 --> 00:16:05.121
on their criminal
justice system.

00:16:05.197 --> 00:16:08.530
It all supports
what Joleg told me.

00:16:08.600 --> 00:16:10.830
Neelix...

00:16:10.903 --> 00:16:12.165
I know what you're thinking.

00:16:12.237 --> 00:16:13.499
That you're the softest touch

00:16:13.572 --> 00:16:14.903
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:16:15.007 --> 00:16:18.135
These are the transcripts
from Joleg's trial.

00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:21.304
He was convicted
on circumstantial evidence.

00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:24.110
Let me guess. He was in the
wrong place at the wrong time.

00:16:24.183 --> 00:16:25.775
Apparently.

00:16:25.851 --> 00:16:28.786
Neelix, when I was
in the Federation penal colony,

00:16:28.854 --> 00:16:30.151
everybody had a story.

00:16:30.222 --> 00:16:33.555
I never put much stock in them.
Neither should you.

00:16:33.625 --> 00:16:37.493
How many of those people
were sentenced to die?

00:16:45.037 --> 00:16:46.766
I still don't understand.

00:16:46.839 --> 00:16:49.273
Why weren't you hurt?

00:16:49.341 --> 00:16:51.104
Because my matrix is photonic.

00:16:51.176 --> 00:16:53.576
I'm made of light.

00:16:53.645 --> 00:16:55.806
You wanted to see me?

00:16:55.881 --> 00:16:57.314
I'll be with you
in just a moment.

00:16:57.383 --> 00:16:59.544
You don't feel pain?

00:16:59.618 --> 00:17:04.487
Well, I suppose my pride
has been wounded on occasion.

00:17:06.158 --> 00:17:08.183
I wish I was made of light.

00:17:10.362 --> 00:17:11.624
Try to rest.

00:17:13.665 --> 00:17:16.395
Mr. Iko responded so well to
the first dose of nanoprobes,

00:17:16.468 --> 00:17:19.096
I thought a second might
improve his condition further.

00:17:19.171 --> 00:17:21.435
It'll only take a
moment to extract them.

00:17:25.611 --> 00:17:28.910
You and Mr. Iko seem to
be getting along well.

00:17:29.048 --> 00:17:30.538
It's the strangest thing.

00:17:30.616 --> 00:17:33.551
When he first arrived,
he was crude, abusive.

00:17:33.619 --> 00:17:36.884
Now he's a model patient...
grateful, considerate.

00:17:36.955 --> 00:17:38.923
He's obviously an
unstable individual.

00:17:39.024 --> 00:17:41.356
Inconsistent behavior
is hardly surprising.

00:17:41.427 --> 00:17:43.918
Still, if it weren't
for the security detail

00:17:44.029 --> 00:17:45.656
I'd forget he
was a criminal.

00:17:45.731 --> 00:17:48.825
It's possible he's trying
to manipulate you.

00:17:48.901 --> 00:17:50.562
Doctor!

00:17:56.075 --> 00:17:57.235
What's the matter?

00:17:57.309 --> 00:17:58.708
My stomach.

00:18:01.647 --> 00:18:03.239
I'm not detecting
anything.

00:18:03.315 --> 00:18:05.442
I... I can't...

00:18:05.517 --> 00:18:07.144
What's wrong?

00:18:07.219 --> 00:18:10.677
I... I can't stop
thinking about...

00:18:10.756 --> 00:18:12.383
the man I killed.

00:18:12.458 --> 00:18:13.686
That's not surprising.

00:18:13.759 --> 00:18:15.420
You're experiencing guilt.

00:18:15.494 --> 00:18:18.122
Is that why I'm feeling sick?

00:18:18.197 --> 00:18:21.098
Nausea could be
a symptom of guilt.

00:18:21.166 --> 00:18:23.327
I've never felt guilty before.

00:18:23.402 --> 00:18:25.461
You've committed many crimes.

00:18:25.537 --> 00:18:27.937
None of them
made me feel like this.

00:18:30.008 --> 00:18:32.340
Why did you do this to me?

00:18:32.411 --> 00:18:34.902
We're not responsible
for your guilt.

00:18:35.013 --> 00:18:37.743
I didn't feel this way,

00:18:37.816 --> 00:18:40.842
until you put
those nanoprobes in me.

00:18:40.919 --> 00:18:43.080
You knew this would happen,

00:18:43.155 --> 00:18:44.622
didn't you?

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:46.920
This is some kind

00:18:47.059 --> 00:18:48.890
of punishment.

00:18:51.864 --> 00:18:54.526
Take the nanoprobes out.

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:55.862
You could die.

00:18:57.569 --> 00:18:59.196
Please?

00:18:59.271 --> 00:19:03.765
I don't want to feel
this way anymore.

00:19:12.918 --> 00:19:14.249
You don't honestly believe

00:19:14.319 --> 00:19:16.219
we're responsible
for his condition.

00:19:16.288 --> 00:19:17.880
We applied the
Borg technology.

00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:19.252
It's possible there were

00:19:19.324 --> 00:19:20.882
some unforeseen side effects.

00:19:20.959 --> 00:19:22.620
Guilt, for example.

00:19:26.398 --> 00:19:27.660
Look at this.

00:19:27.733 --> 00:19:29.166
What?

00:19:29.234 --> 00:19:30.667
It's my most recent scan.

00:19:30.736 --> 00:19:32.897
The neurotransmitters
have established

00:19:33.038 --> 00:19:35.404
new pathways
throughout his cortex.

00:19:35.474 --> 00:19:37.442
Wasn't that your intention?

00:19:37.509 --> 00:19:39.204
No, I was simply trying

00:19:39.278 --> 00:19:40.768
to bypass the edema.

00:19:40.846 --> 00:19:42.711
Then how did this happen?

00:19:42.781 --> 00:19:44.043
I don't know.

00:19:44.116 --> 00:19:46.880
It's possible this is normal
Nygean brain activity,

00:19:46.952 --> 00:19:49.512
but I have no basis
for comparison.

00:19:49.588 --> 00:19:51.351
You should ask Mr. Yediq

00:19:51.423 --> 00:19:53.914
to contact
a Nygean medical official.

00:19:53.992 --> 00:19:57.553
Maybe they could provide
some relevant information.

00:20:03.769 --> 00:20:06.033
Seven of Nine.

00:20:06.104 --> 00:20:07.571
Stay?

00:20:07.639 --> 00:20:09.038
Talk to me.

00:20:09.107 --> 00:20:10.734
I'm extremely busy.

00:20:10.809 --> 00:20:13.039
Please.

00:20:13.111 --> 00:20:14.703
I'm scared.

00:20:20.118 --> 00:20:22.086
What did you want to discuss?

00:20:25.691 --> 00:20:28.717
I'm due in Astrometrics,
so if there's nothing...

00:20:28.794 --> 00:20:30.625
Astrometrics... what's that?

00:20:30.696 --> 00:20:33.859
A laboratory where
we observe stellar phenomena.

00:20:33.932 --> 00:20:36.560
When I was a child,

00:20:36.635 --> 00:20:40.594
I'd... lie under the stars
for hours.

00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:44.870
I'd stare at them
until I could see the shapes.

00:20:44.943 --> 00:20:46.570
Shapes?

00:20:46.645 --> 00:20:50.775
Faces and animals
made out of stars.

00:20:50.849 --> 00:20:54.080
You're referring
to constellations.

00:20:54.152 --> 00:20:56.746
I named them.

00:20:56.822 --> 00:20:59.256
There was
Paedos the Warrior

00:20:59.324 --> 00:21:05.194
and Gezid the Beast.

00:21:05.264 --> 00:21:07.698
No matter how hard he tried,

00:21:07.766 --> 00:21:11.258
Paedos could never catch Gezid.

00:21:11.336 --> 00:21:14.772
Because the distance between
them always remained the same.

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:17.900
You've seen them?

00:21:17.976 --> 00:21:20.035
Possibly.

00:21:20.112 --> 00:21:23.172
I've cataloged approximately
six billion stars.

00:21:23.248 --> 00:21:28.311
Then you must have seen Onella,
too... the Mother.

00:21:30.622 --> 00:21:32.556
Describe her.

00:21:32.624 --> 00:21:35.115
She was surrounded

00:21:35.193 --> 00:21:38.253
by 16 smaller stars...

00:21:38.330 --> 00:21:40.264
her daughters.

00:21:40.332 --> 00:21:42.129
If I try, I think

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:45.499
I can remember
all their names.

00:21:49.207 --> 00:21:52.176
Grid 11-6. Green.

00:21:52.244 --> 00:21:53.711
What's going on over there?

00:21:53.779 --> 00:21:54.871
Kot-Kot.

00:21:56.281 --> 00:21:57.942
That's Kadis-Kot.

00:21:58.016 --> 00:21:59.540
Congratulations.

00:21:59.618 --> 00:22:02.212
Down here.

00:22:03.588 --> 00:22:05.681
I've been doing some research

00:22:05.757 --> 00:22:07.691
on the Nygean legal system.

00:22:07.759 --> 00:22:09.192
You were right

00:22:09.261 --> 00:22:12.526
about the Benkarans
receiving harsher sentences.

00:22:12.597 --> 00:22:14.531
I saw the statistics.

00:22:14.599 --> 00:22:17.534
Statistics won't save me.

00:22:17.602 --> 00:22:21.060
I noticed some people
convicted of murder...

00:22:21.139 --> 00:22:25.041
even terrible, premeditated
murders... weren't executed.

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:27.135
Some weren't punished at all,

00:22:27.212 --> 00:22:28.941
but you were
sentenced to death.

00:22:29.081 --> 00:22:30.708
That's what the family wants.

00:22:30.782 --> 00:22:32.545
The family?

00:22:32.617 --> 00:22:34.551
After you're convicted,

00:22:34.619 --> 00:22:37.349
the family of the
victim sentences you.

00:22:37.422 --> 00:22:41.085
Well, shouldn't you be sentenced
by someone less partial,

00:22:41.159 --> 00:22:42.888
like a judge?

00:22:42.961 --> 00:22:46.055
Vekto valek k'vadim.

00:22:46.131 --> 00:22:48.065
It's Ancient Nygean.

00:22:48.133 --> 00:22:50.067
It means, "Favor the victims."

00:22:52.170 --> 00:22:56.334
What if I stole your game board?

00:22:56.408 --> 00:23:00.504
What right would a judge have
to assign value to your loss?

00:23:00.579 --> 00:23:02.513
To him, it's just a game board,

00:23:02.581 --> 00:23:05.914
but to you it might be
a priceless family possession.

00:23:07.819 --> 00:23:10.117
And what
if I murdered your child?

00:23:13.458 --> 00:23:15.688
I think I get your point.

00:23:15.761 --> 00:23:18.355
Vekto valek k'vadim.

00:23:18.430 --> 00:23:21.558
It's the basis for the
Nygean legal system.

00:23:21.633 --> 00:23:23.066
What about the criminals

00:23:23.135 --> 00:23:25.103
that didn't serve
any sentence at all?

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:29.937
Some people prefer
restitution to revenge.

00:23:30.041 --> 00:23:33.238
If a defendant is
wealthy enough,

00:23:33.311 --> 00:23:36.109
he can negotiate a settlement
with the victim's family.

00:23:36.181 --> 00:23:39.275
Oh, that doesn't seem fair.

00:23:39.351 --> 00:23:43.287
It's perfectly fair,
unless you're destitute.

00:23:46.124 --> 00:23:48.615
Maybe I can talk to the Captain

00:23:48.693 --> 00:23:52.493
about finding a way
to compensate your victims.

00:23:52.564 --> 00:23:54.964
I'm grateful...

00:23:55.066 --> 00:23:57.864
but it would imply I'm guilty.

00:23:59.070 --> 00:24:00.799
I wouldn't want that.

00:24:03.074 --> 00:24:05.338
There must
be something I can do.

00:24:07.846 --> 00:24:10.110
You can transmit a letter
to my brother.

00:24:10.182 --> 00:24:13.674
I'd like to let him know
what's happened to me.

00:24:13.752 --> 00:24:15.879
I'll get a padd.

00:24:30.101 --> 00:24:33.070
I thought you might
find this interesting.

00:24:37.609 --> 00:24:39.042
What is it?

00:24:39.110 --> 00:24:40.873
It's an Astrometrics log.

00:24:40.946 --> 00:24:42.470
It contains data

00:24:42.547 --> 00:24:44.811
on various star formations.

00:24:46.885 --> 00:24:49.513
It's just words and numbers.

00:24:49.588 --> 00:24:52.318
I'd rather look at the stars.

00:24:52.390 --> 00:24:55.826
I'll bring you a star chart

00:24:55.894 --> 00:24:57.657
after my next shift.

00:25:05.237 --> 00:25:07.330
What's the metal above your eye?

00:25:07.405 --> 00:25:10.340
It's a cybernetic implant.

00:25:10.408 --> 00:25:11.875
Where did you get it?

00:25:11.943 --> 00:25:14.173
It was installed by the Borg.

00:25:14.246 --> 00:25:16.180
Must have hurt.

00:25:16.248 --> 00:25:19.308
I don't recall.

00:25:22.087 --> 00:25:24.555
I hurt people.

00:25:26.925 --> 00:25:29.587
I deserve to die.

00:25:30.929 --> 00:25:32.521
Seven?

00:25:32.597 --> 00:25:34.895
I found something.

00:25:45.343 --> 00:25:48.506
This is a scan depicting
a healthy Nygean brain.

00:25:48.580 --> 00:25:51.174
This node is analogous

00:25:51.249 --> 00:25:52.546
to the human pineal gland.

00:25:52.617 --> 00:25:54.949
In addition to controlling
behavioral impulses,

00:25:55.053 --> 00:25:56.543
it regulates decision making.

00:25:56.621 --> 00:25:57.883
You might say

00:25:57.956 --> 00:25:59.947
it's the physiological
equivalent of a conscience.

00:26:00.058 --> 00:26:02.686
Normally, the node connects
to the rest of the brain

00:26:02.761 --> 00:26:04.592
through a series
of neural pathways.

00:26:04.663 --> 00:26:05.891
Now...

00:26:05.997 --> 00:26:07.726
Iook at the scan of lko's node

00:26:07.799 --> 00:26:09.699
before we applied
the nanoprobes.

00:26:09.768 --> 00:26:11.326
It's detached.

00:26:11.403 --> 00:26:13.337
Did that happen
when he was assaulted?

00:26:13.405 --> 00:26:15.999
No. I believe it's
congenital... a birth defect.

00:26:16.074 --> 00:26:19.202
Without the node, lko would
have been prone to violence

00:26:19.277 --> 00:26:21.177
and sociopathic
behavior all his life.

00:26:21.246 --> 00:26:22.679
When I used
Seven's nanoprobes

00:26:22.747 --> 00:26:24.544
to treat the injuries
from the assault,

00:26:24.616 --> 00:26:27.551
it seems they inadvertently
repaired the defect, as well.

00:26:27.619 --> 00:26:29.348
You've activated his conscience.

00:26:29.421 --> 00:26:30.854
Well, that would explain

00:26:30.922 --> 00:26:32.753
why he's suddenly
experiencing guilt.

00:26:32.824 --> 00:26:34.257
There's more to it than that.

00:26:34.326 --> 00:26:36.920
I believe he's become capable
of controlling

00:26:36.995 --> 00:26:38.519
his violent impulses.

00:26:38.597 --> 00:26:40.588
Capable, maybe,

00:26:40.665 --> 00:26:42.223
but how do you know he will?

00:26:42.300 --> 00:26:45.064
Even the thought of violence
makes him ill now.

00:26:45.136 --> 00:26:48.071
In my opinion, he's no longer
a threat to anyone.

00:26:48.139 --> 00:26:50.334
By some definitions, Captain,

00:26:50.408 --> 00:26:53.002
he's not the same man
who committed the murder.

00:27:01.252 --> 00:27:03.311
Are you suggesting
we release him?

00:27:03.388 --> 00:27:05.413
Of course not,
but at the very least,

00:27:05.490 --> 00:27:07.219
his case should
be reexamined.

00:27:07.292 --> 00:27:08.782
Because he's sorry.

00:27:08.860 --> 00:27:11.021
There's new medical
evidence to be considered.

00:27:11.096 --> 00:27:13.997
None of it changes the fact
that he killed a man.

00:27:14.065 --> 00:27:15.896
He was suffering
from a neurological defect.

00:27:16.001 --> 00:27:17.400
He couldn't control
his behavior.

00:27:17.469 --> 00:27:19.232
If lko had been diagnosed
and treated,

00:27:19.304 --> 00:27:21.329
he never would have committed
that crime.

00:27:21.406 --> 00:27:22.703
In a manner of speaking,

00:27:22.774 --> 00:27:24.435
he's a victim
of his own biology.

00:27:24.509 --> 00:27:26.204
So lko is the victim now?

00:27:26.277 --> 00:27:27.904
No one's denying

00:27:28.046 --> 00:27:31.209
that he committed
a terrible crime,

00:27:31.282 --> 00:27:33.807
but as a result
of the Doctor's treatments,

00:27:33.885 --> 00:27:36.046
he's undergone
a fundamental change.

00:27:36.121 --> 00:27:38.419
Killing him
won't accomplish anything.

00:27:38.490 --> 00:27:40.321
That's not your decision
to make.

00:27:40.392 --> 00:27:41.723
Nor is it yours.

00:27:41.793 --> 00:27:44.023
He's obviously
deceiving you somehow.

00:27:44.095 --> 00:27:46.325
Listen, we could debate this
all day,

00:27:46.398 --> 00:27:49.856
but the fact is, our personal
opinions are irrelevant.

00:27:49.934 --> 00:27:51.925
All that matters is Nygean law.

00:27:52.003 --> 00:27:55.495
Does lko have a legal means
of appeal at his disposal?

00:27:55.573 --> 00:27:59.304
In accordance
with Nygean Penal Code,

00:27:59.377 --> 00:28:02.835
a capital defendant has a right
to appeal his sentence

00:28:02.914 --> 00:28:04.779
to the family of his victims.

00:28:04.849 --> 00:28:06.874
Then I'd like you
to help Commander Tuvok

00:28:07.018 --> 00:28:08.713
draft an appeal

00:28:08.787 --> 00:28:10.550
and submit it
to the proper authorities.

00:28:16.227 --> 00:28:18.161
Take back the appeal.

00:28:18.229 --> 00:28:19.526
You'd rather die,

00:28:19.597 --> 00:28:21.724
because you think
it'll relieve your pain?

00:28:23.768 --> 00:28:26.828
Death is what I deserve.

00:28:26.905 --> 00:28:28.463
You say I've changed,

00:28:28.540 --> 00:28:31.168
but I look at these hands
every day,

00:28:31.242 --> 00:28:34.575
and I see them squeezing
that man's throat,

00:28:34.646 --> 00:28:38.013
and I hear the
sounds he made.

00:28:41.319 --> 00:28:43.514
I'm disgusting.

00:28:46.124 --> 00:28:48.786
Do you think I'm disgusting?

00:28:50.328 --> 00:28:54.059
You've been nothing
but kind to me.

00:28:54.132 --> 00:28:56.760
You asked me earlier
if it hurt

00:28:56.835 --> 00:28:59.827
when my occipital implant
was installed.

00:28:59.904 --> 00:29:03.840
I told you I didn't remember,

00:29:03.908 --> 00:29:06.502
but the truth is...

00:29:06.578 --> 00:29:10.139
it was one of the most painful
experiences of my life.

00:29:10.215 --> 00:29:13.275
Why did you lie?

00:29:16.888 --> 00:29:21.325
It's difficult for me
to talk about,

00:29:21.392 --> 00:29:24.486
because I forced others
to undergo the same procedure.

00:29:24.562 --> 00:29:25.494
Why?

00:29:25.563 --> 00:29:26.860
I was compelled to do so

00:29:26.931 --> 00:29:28.660
by the Borg collective.

00:29:28.733 --> 00:29:31.167
I wasn't in control
of my actions,

00:29:31.236 --> 00:29:35.070
just as you weren't in control
when you took a life.

00:29:35.140 --> 00:29:39.406
My nanoprobes
have given you control.

00:29:39.477 --> 00:29:40.910
You're a different person now.

00:29:41.012 --> 00:29:42.639
You don't deserve
to be executed.

00:29:54.159 --> 00:29:55.786
I want to go back to my cell.

00:29:55.860 --> 00:29:57.555
You're free to remain here.

00:29:57.629 --> 00:29:59.153
Am I still sick?

00:29:59.230 --> 00:30:00.788
No, but...

00:30:00.865 --> 00:30:03.459
Then I don't want
special treatment.

00:30:16.181 --> 00:30:18.274
I'm glad to see
you're feeling better.

00:30:20.819 --> 00:30:22.980
You must be hungry.

00:30:36.301 --> 00:30:37.461
Here you go.

00:30:37.535 --> 00:30:38.695
Give it to him.

00:30:42.507 --> 00:30:43.735
He's already had his dinner.

00:30:43.808 --> 00:30:46.402
Please.

00:30:48.179 --> 00:30:50.511
All right.

00:31:11.970 --> 00:31:13.904
You wanted to see me.

00:31:13.972 --> 00:31:18.500
We just received a response
from the Nygeans.

00:31:18.576 --> 00:31:21.477
The family has refused
to consider the appeal.

00:31:21.546 --> 00:31:24.413
But the medical evidence...

00:31:24.482 --> 00:31:26.245
They won't look at it.

00:31:26.317 --> 00:31:28.444
The family
found the request insulting.

00:31:28.519 --> 00:31:30.612
Your government could insist
that they review it.

00:31:30.688 --> 00:31:35.091
We have laws that protect
victims from emotional distress.

00:31:35.159 --> 00:31:38.287
In that case, we should grant
lko asylum aboard Voyager.

00:31:38.363 --> 00:31:40.228
You agreed to work

00:31:40.298 --> 00:31:42.289
within the confines
of our legal system.

00:31:42.367 --> 00:31:43.959
Your system is flawed.

00:31:44.035 --> 00:31:45.297
That's enough, Seven.

00:31:46.738 --> 00:31:52.267
I assure you, we'll abide
by the family's decision.

00:31:52.343 --> 00:31:56.177
Now, I need a moment alone
with Seven, if you don't mind?

00:32:01.753 --> 00:32:03.721
We did everything we could
to help him.

00:32:03.788 --> 00:32:05.449
We have to do more.

00:32:05.523 --> 00:32:06.854
You barely know this man.

00:32:06.925 --> 00:32:09.291
Why are you so passionate
about helping him?

00:32:09.360 --> 00:32:12.420
I want to give him the same
opportunity you gave me.

00:32:12.497 --> 00:32:16.263
When you severed my
link to the collective,

00:32:16.334 --> 00:32:17.824
you changed who I was.

00:32:17.902 --> 00:32:21.463
You made it possible for me
to reclaim my humanity.

00:32:21.539 --> 00:32:25.407
Because of my nanoprobes, lko
has undergone a similar change.

00:32:25.476 --> 00:32:28.877
He should be given the chance
to atone for his crimes.

00:32:28.947 --> 00:32:32.508
Atonement?
Is that what this is about?

00:32:32.583 --> 00:32:33.811
Yes.

00:32:33.885 --> 00:32:37.048
For him... or for you?

00:32:37.121 --> 00:32:39.851
I don't know what you mean.

00:32:39.924 --> 00:32:42.620
I think part of you
still feels responsible

00:32:42.694 --> 00:32:46.289
for the violent acts you
committed when you were a Borg.

00:32:46.364 --> 00:32:47.524
You're mistaken.

00:32:47.598 --> 00:32:49.964
Am I?

00:32:50.101 --> 00:32:54.504
Maybe you believe
if lko is found not guilty,

00:32:54.572 --> 00:32:56.369
somehow you won't
be guilty, either.

00:32:56.441 --> 00:32:59.205
You said it yourself.

00:32:59.277 --> 00:33:00.801
You've reclaimed your humanity.

00:33:00.878 --> 00:33:02.903
It's time you stopped
blaming yourself

00:33:02.981 --> 00:33:04.710
for the crimes
of the collective.

00:33:12.090 --> 00:33:13.318
Report.

00:33:13.391 --> 00:33:16.121
An alien vessel just dropped
out of warp and opened fire.

00:33:39.050 --> 00:33:43.043
We've lost power
on Decks 8 through 10.

00:33:43.121 --> 00:33:44.110
The cargo bay.

00:33:50.728 --> 00:33:52.355
Hurry, hurry!

00:33:52.430 --> 00:33:54.398
Follow me.
Let's go to the Bridge.

00:33:54.465 --> 00:33:55.432
Keep 'em down!

00:34:00.905 --> 00:34:01.997
Hurry.

00:34:04.308 --> 00:34:06.674
There's a corridor...

00:34:06.744 --> 00:34:07.870
Stay together.

00:34:21.759 --> 00:34:23.693
Shields down to 60 percent.

00:34:23.761 --> 00:34:25.388
Still no response to hails.

00:34:25.463 --> 00:34:26.623
Evasive maneuvers.

00:34:26.697 --> 00:34:28.028
Target their weapons.

00:34:41.846 --> 00:34:43.609
Tuvok to Bridge.
The attacking ship

00:34:43.681 --> 00:34:45.911
is attempting to transport
one of the prisoners.

00:34:45.983 --> 00:34:48.781
They're trying to lock on to all
five Benkaran life signs.

00:34:51.055 --> 00:34:52.784
Target their transporter array.

00:34:57.895 --> 00:34:58.827
Direct hit.

00:34:58.896 --> 00:35:00.363
They're retreating.

00:35:00.431 --> 00:35:01.864
Pursuit course?

00:35:01.933 --> 00:35:03.127
No, we have
more immediate problems.

00:35:03.201 --> 00:35:04.498
Bridge to Tuvok.
What's your status?

00:35:05.770 --> 00:35:08.000
We've neutralized
two of the prisoners.

00:35:10.308 --> 00:35:12.435
Someone's trying to get
into the Shuttle Bay.

00:35:12.510 --> 00:35:13.704
Lock them out.

00:35:16.114 --> 00:35:17.809
Again.

00:35:18.883 --> 00:35:20.248
Stand back!

00:35:24.555 --> 00:35:26.682
Don't move.

00:35:34.665 --> 00:35:38.192
You have five minutes
to get us a shuttle.

00:35:39.971 --> 00:35:41.097
Tuvok to Bridge.

00:35:41.172 --> 00:35:43.231
Lock on to Yediq's
signature, and beam him to...

00:35:43.307 --> 00:35:44.638
Transporters are off-line.

00:35:44.709 --> 00:35:47.678
We need at least ten minutes
to get them up and running.

00:35:55.153 --> 00:35:56.780
Seal it.

00:36:00.525 --> 00:36:01.890
You're not getting off

00:36:01.959 --> 00:36:03.085
this ship.

00:36:03.161 --> 00:36:05.755
Then I suppose I should kill you
right now.

00:36:08.533 --> 00:36:09.659
Don't!

00:36:16.541 --> 00:36:17.872
He's mine.

00:36:25.616 --> 00:36:27.982
You saw how they beat me.

00:36:39.197 --> 00:36:41.165
I knew it was a trick.

00:36:41.232 --> 00:36:43.666
I knew you hadn't changed.

00:37:10.061 --> 00:37:12.291
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:37:12.363 --> 00:37:14.627
Warden Yediq has used
his influence

00:37:14.699 --> 00:37:16.599
to convince the Nygean family

00:37:16.667 --> 00:37:19.602
to hear lko's appeal
for leniency.

00:37:21.505 --> 00:37:23.666
I won't beg for my life.

00:37:23.741 --> 00:37:25.368
It belongs to you.

00:37:25.443 --> 00:37:32.144
I only want you to understand
what's happened to me.

00:37:32.216 --> 00:37:35.117
I'm a different person now...

00:37:35.186 --> 00:37:37.916
a better person.

00:37:38.022 --> 00:37:44.825
This crew...
has helped me to see that.

00:37:56.974 --> 00:37:59.875
If my death
helps you find peace,

00:37:59.944 --> 00:38:02.742
I can accept it.

00:38:02.813 --> 00:38:04.804
But if you let me live,

00:38:04.882 --> 00:38:10.047
I will never hurt anyone again.

00:38:12.923 --> 00:38:16.586
Whatever you decide,

00:38:16.661 --> 00:38:21.724
please know how sorry I am

00:38:21.799 --> 00:38:25.064
for what I took from you.

00:38:29.940 --> 00:38:31.840
Are we playing
Kadis-Kot later?

00:38:31.909 --> 00:38:33.536
Sorry.

00:38:33.611 --> 00:38:36.273
Afraid I'll beat you again?

00:38:36.347 --> 00:38:38.372
I tried to help you,

00:38:38.449 --> 00:38:40.417
and you took advantage of me.

00:38:40.484 --> 00:38:42.645
What do you mean?

00:38:42.720 --> 00:38:44.915
The note we sent your brother.

00:38:45.022 --> 00:38:47.582
He traced the transmission
to Voyager.

00:38:47.658 --> 00:38:49.558
He's the one who attacked us.

00:38:49.627 --> 00:38:53.586
Neelix, I swear I had no idea

00:38:53.664 --> 00:38:55.655
he would do that.

00:38:55.733 --> 00:38:57.166
You have to believe me.

00:38:57.234 --> 00:39:00.067
I read Yediq's security report.

00:39:00.137 --> 00:39:01.764
You threatened to kill him.

00:39:06.143 --> 00:39:07.735
I can't eat this.

00:39:07.812 --> 00:39:09.143
Why not?

00:39:09.213 --> 00:39:11.340
I'm sick.

00:39:11.415 --> 00:39:13.645
You look fine to me.

00:39:13.718 --> 00:39:17.882
No, I must have
the same condition lko had.

00:39:20.358 --> 00:39:23.589
If your Doctor cures me,

00:39:23.661 --> 00:39:25.959
I can make an appeal
for my life, too.

00:39:37.675 --> 00:39:39.540
She's beautiful, isn't she?

00:39:39.610 --> 00:39:42.272
Onella, the Mother?

00:39:46.250 --> 00:39:49.117
And there's Paedos...

00:39:49.186 --> 00:39:51.154
still watching over her.

00:39:55.259 --> 00:39:57.352
It was kind of
Captain Janeway

00:39:57.428 --> 00:39:59.191
to let you bring me here.

00:39:59.263 --> 00:40:00.491
If your appeal is successful,

00:40:00.564 --> 00:40:02.293
you'll be able to go
wherever you want.

00:40:02.366 --> 00:40:04.857
I hope you're right.

00:40:04.935 --> 00:40:06.994
If I am, where will you go?

00:40:10.274 --> 00:40:11.866
I don't know.

00:40:11.942 --> 00:40:13.034
If you'd like,

00:40:13.110 --> 00:40:14.338
I could ask Captain Janeway

00:40:14.412 --> 00:40:16.471
to consider
letting you stay here.

00:40:16.547 --> 00:40:18.310
I'm not a scientist.

00:40:18.382 --> 00:40:22.079
I don't think
I'd be much help to anyone.

00:40:22.153 --> 00:40:24.917
There are other ways
to be useful.

00:40:24.989 --> 00:40:26.547
I'm sure we could think
of something.

00:40:26.624 --> 00:40:29.821
I'd like that.

00:40:37.368 --> 00:40:39.393
I'm sorry.

00:40:39.470 --> 00:40:43.531
The family has denied
your appeal.

00:40:43.607 --> 00:40:45.370
We're due to rendezvous

00:40:45.443 --> 00:40:48.378
with a transport
ship in a few hours.

00:40:48.446 --> 00:40:52.382
I need to return
you to your cell.

00:41:02.059 --> 00:41:04.527
You were the first person

00:41:04.595 --> 00:41:06.825
who wasn't afraid
to look me in the eye.

00:41:08.666 --> 00:41:11.226
That's how I'd like
to remember you.

00:41:51.175 --> 00:41:53.973
I just finished looking over
your warp core analysis.

00:41:54.078 --> 00:41:54.976
And?

00:41:55.079 --> 00:41:56.205
I'm impressed.

00:41:56.280 --> 00:41:58.373
It usually takes a few days
to finish one of these.

00:41:58.449 --> 00:42:00.280
B'Elanna tells me
you did it in 22 hours.

00:42:00.351 --> 00:42:04.151
I haven't felt the need
to regenerate.

00:42:04.221 --> 00:42:07.987
Everyone grieves
in their own way.

00:42:12.963 --> 00:42:13.930
If you want to talk,

00:42:14.064 --> 00:42:16.032
you know where to find me.

00:42:18.068 --> 00:42:19.865
It's unfair.

00:42:19.937 --> 00:42:22.838
I think so, too, Seven...

00:42:22.907 --> 00:42:26.172
but we have to try not
to judge their system.

00:42:26.243 --> 00:42:29.576
That's not what I meant.

00:42:29.647 --> 00:42:33.208
Iko was executed
for taking a single life.

00:42:33.284 --> 00:42:36.412
As a drone,
I took thousands,

00:42:36.487 --> 00:42:39.479
but I was never punished.

00:42:45.262 --> 00:42:50.131
You lost 20 years of
your life to the Borg.

00:42:50.200 --> 00:42:52.964
I'd say that's
punishment enough.
